.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt CTAGS 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm ctags
.Nd build a tags file for C definitions
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl x
.Op Fl f Ar file
.Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility scans C source files and writes functions, top-level globals,
.Cm #define
macros,
.Cm struct
tags and
.Cm enum
tags.
The default output is
.Pa tags
with one
.Ar name Ns \t Ns Ar file Ns \t Ns Ar line
record per definition, sorted by name.
.Pp
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl f Ar file
Write the tags file to
.Ar file .
.Ar -
writes to standard output.
.It Fl x
Write a cross-reference listing to standard output instead:
.Ar name Ns \t Ns Ar line Ns \t Ns Ar file Ns \t Ns Ar source-line .
.El
.Pp
The analyzer is lexical: it does not evaluate the preprocessor, types or expressions.
.Fl t ,
.Fl u ,
.Fl v
and
.Fl w
are unsupported.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
0 on success, 1 for a file or output error, 2 for usage.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr cflow 1 ,
.Xr cxref 1
.Sh STANDARDS
A documented subset of POSIX
.Nm ctags .
Standard input, C++, typedef aliases, struct members, enum constants and function-pointer
declarators are unsupported.
